Subject: [PATCH] audio: align audioPortParam field to reference (attr)

The reference SDK (CellAudioPortParam) and current upstream PSL1GHT use
'attr'; our vendored PSL1GHT header had the stale 'attrib'. Anonymous
union exposes both names (identical single-u64 layout) so 5ba78ae samples
(.attr) build with zero breakage for any legacy .attrib user.

diff --git a/ppu/include/audio/audio.h b/ppu/include/audio/audio.h
index 00a6fb4..8c83334 100644
--- a/ppu/include/audio/audio.h
+++ b/ppu/include/audio/audio.h
@@ -96,7 +96,14 @@ typedef struct _audio_port_param
 
 	This value must be either 0 or \ref AUDIO_PORT_INITLEVEL.
 	*/
-	u64 attrib;
+	/* Field name aligned to the reference SDK (CellAudioPortParam.attr) and
+	 * current upstream PSL1GHT, which renamed the old `attrib`.  Anonymous
+	 * union keeps the legacy `attrib` spelling working with zero breakage;
+	 * identical single-u64 layout. */
+	union {
+		u64 attr;
+		u64 attrib;
+	};
 
 	/*! \Brief Initial volume.
 
